y and are trading days in both libraries. No BSX notice for those days was read, and a public holiday is not an exchange closure without the exchange's word, so the eight dates (21 June 2010 ... 19 June 2017) are not added; recent BSX notices do close the exchange 'in observance of' each public holiday. 2025-2026: exchange_calendars + exchange_publications. 2027-2029: standing pattern. Checked 2026-11-20 (4c11). Last published year: BSX's festive notice for 2025/2026 (https://www.bsx.com/bermuda-stock-exchange-20252026-festive-holiday-closure-notice, 18 December 2025) gives 24 December 2025 as an early closure 9:00am-2:00pm and 31 December 2025 as normal operating hours (9:00am-5:00pm). The registry had both as early closes at 13:00: 2025-12-24 now closes at 14:00 and cites the notice, the 31 December early closes for 2025, 2026, 2027 and 2029 are removed (2024 and 2025 were both normal days), and 24 December 2026, 2027 and 2029 are predicted early closes at 14:00. 24 December 2026 is unconfirmed with recheck_date 2026-12-22 (the 2025 notice came on 18 December). BSX's holiday notices for 2025-2026 (Bermuda Day, Remembrance Day, Good Friday, Cup Match) match the registry. Close (ADR 0013): BSX's trading page (https://www.bsx.com/trading/trading) says 'Trading Hours are Monday through Friday 9:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m. (Atlantic Time)'; BSX trades continuously after an 08:30-09:00 price discovery phase (hurricane and Carter notices) with no closing auction, so the close is the end of continuous trading, 16:30. regular_hours is 09:00-16:30 (was 10:00-16:00; exchange_calendars has 09:00-16:30), one dated entry from 2010-01-01, unconfirmed: press (Bernews, 23 September 2016) reports the 16:30 close took effect on 28 September 2016, after an earlier close; BSX's own announcement was not read, so no earlier entry is dated. Price discovery is not modelled.",
